    "done_when": "A new tests/test_a_follower_runs_current_code.py shows the four cases §107 lists, with a temporary home and a stubbed checkout: a subscriber follower whose source checkout's stamp differs from its own, with the checkout trusted, re-executes, counted through a patch on the exec call; one whose stamp matches, or whose checkout is not trusted, does not; one started from a reload tree with _FOLLOWER_SOURCE_ROOT_ENV naming the original checkout compares against that checkout, not the tree it imports from; and over a hundred sweeps spanning three of the reloader's checked_at intervals, with its stamp matching, the subscriber reads the checkout's identity exactly three times, counted through a patch on the identity read. The file fails at the base and passes at the head. Two negative controls, each applied and logged under the run directory's logs/: restoring reloader = None on the subscriber path makes the stale-stamp case record no exec, and dropping the trust check makes the untrusted case re-execute. tests/test_follower_freshness.py passes at head, its docstring updated where the behaviour it states changes. baseline_suite and after_suite are run with the project's armed suite command at the base and the head. Every test file that imports reckon.crew_follow_commands or reckon.crew.follower_reload adds no failure against a base arm, from git archive trees with the main checkout's .env linked, -n 6 at most. Every log is under the run directory, starts with its revision, tree and literal command, and ends in EXIT=. ruff check and ruff format --check add no findings on the staged paths. Run everything in the foreground on the fleet allocation.",
